    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: agyx-dev-architect\ndescription: Architect and optimize 120fps Android apps (AgyX-V2, opencode-mobile) across Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and Rust JNI native cores.\nwhen_not_to_use: Web-only HTML/CSS tasks, CI YAML edits, or Termux shell setup.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [kotlin, compose, 120fps, jni, ffi, libagyx_core, unwrap, sigabrt]\n---\n# AgyX & Android 120fps Dev Architect (v3)\n\n## 1. 120fps Jetpack Compose Performance Laws\n- **Recomposition Control**: Annotate all UI state classes with `@Immutable` or `@Stable`. Never pass unstable `List`/`Map` directly without wrapping or using `kotlinx.collections.immutable`.\n- **Defer State Reads**: Read fast-changing scroll/gesture/animation states inside lambda modifiers (`Modifier.offset { ... }`, `Modifier.graphicsLayer { ... }`) rather than inside `@Composable` bodies.\n- **Streaming Chat / Terminal Lists**: Use stable `key = { it.id }` in `LazyColumn` and isolate active token-streaming state into a leaf composable so past messages never recompose.\n- **Corner Radius Safety**: Always clamp animated corner radii with `.coerceAtLeast(0.dp)` to prevent native outline crashes.\n\n## 2. Clean Kotlin <-> Rust JNI/FFI Boundaries (`lib*.so`)\n- **Thread Discipline**: Never execute synchronous JNI calls, file I/O, or network parsing on `Dispatchers.Main`; always dispatch to `Dispatchers.IO` or `Dispatchers.Default`.\n- **Zero-Panic FFI**: **FORBIDDEN** to use `.unwrap()` or `.expect()` in `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\"` Rust entry points—a Rust panic across JNI aborts the entire Android process (`SIGABRT`). Return structured `Result` JSON/error codes instead.\n- **Memory Hygiene**: Release `JNIEnv` local references (`GetStringUTFChars` / `ReleaseStringUTFChars`) cleanly in long-running loops.\n\n## 3. Verification Gate\n- Verify JNI method signatures (`Java_package_Class_method`) match Kotlin `external fun` declarations 1:1 and check `./gradlew compileDebugKotlin` or `cargo check --target aarch64-linux-android`.\n",
