    content: "---\nname: domain-modeling\ndescription: Model strict domain types, exhaustive state machines, and boundary invariants in Kotlin, Rust, and TypeScript.\nwhen_not_to_use: CSS styling, shell automation, or CI pipeline config.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [sealed interface, state machine, value class, enum, illegal state]\n---\n# Domain Modeling (v3)\n\n## 1. Type & State Machine Standards\n- **Exhaustive State Machines**: Represent lifecycle states via Kotlin `sealed interface`, Rust `enum`, or TypeScript discriminated unions—never overlapping boolean flags (`isLoading`, `isError`, `isSuccess`).\n- **Zero Primitive Obsession**: Wrap IDs, ports, paths, and tokens in `@JvmInline value class` (Kotlin), newtype structs (Rust), or branded types (TS).\n- **Boundary Mapping**: Keep domain models pure and framework-free; convert raw JSON/SQL/JNI DTOs at the outer boundary and reject invalid states early.\n\n## 2. Hard Invariants\n- **NEVER** allow invalid state combinations to compile when the type system can enforce invariants.\n",
