    content: "---\nname: github-repo-scout\ndescription: Evaluate GitHub repositories for Android/Termux compatibility, extract core architecture, and produce ready-to-run build or porting plans.\nwhen_not_to_use: Files already inside the local workspace or pure UI styling.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [github repo, open-source, bionic, glibc, arm64 compatibility, port]\n---\n# GitHub Repo Scout (v3)\n\n## 1. Android / Termux Blocker Matrix\n- **Prebuilt Linux Release Binaries (`glibc`)**: Fail on native Termux (`bionic` libc) with `No such file or directory`. Fix: compile from source in Termux (`pkg`), build static `musl`, cross-compile via `cargo-ndk`, or run inside Ubuntu `proot`.\n- **Kernel / Root Privileges (`/dev/net/tun`, `iptables`, `mount`)**: Fail on unrooted Android. Fix: check for userspace networking (`gvisor`/`smoltcp`) or rootless flags before adopting.\n- **CPU Architecture (`x86_64` intrinsics)**: Verify `aarch64` / `arm64-v8a` build targets in `Cargo.toml`, `CMakeLists.txt`, or CI workflows.\n\n## 2. Recon & Evaluation Protocol\n1. **Inspect Manifests & CI**: Read `README.md`, `Cargo.toml` / `package.json` / `build.gradle(.kts)`, and `.github/workflows/*` first to see exact toolchains.\n2. **Trace Core Hot Path**: Identify entry points, network/IPC protocol layers, and native bindings without reading bloated lockfiles or vendor folders.\n3. **Deliver Integration Blueprint**: Provide exact `git clone --depth 1` + build commands and specify how to bridge the module into Kotlin/Rust (`lib*.so`) or Termux CLI.\n\n## 3. Hard Invariants\n- **NEVER** recommend raw x86_64 or glibc GitHub release binaries for native Termux without a `proot` or source-build path.\n",
