    content: "---\nname: grilling\ndescription: Stress-test specs, architectures, and diffs with adversarial edge-case probes to expose failure modes before coding.\nwhen_not_to_use: Trivial one-line edits or already-verified production hotfixes.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [stress-test, adversarial, edge-case probe, failure vector, break plan]\n---\n# Grilling (v3)\n\n## 1. Mandatory Stress-Test Vectors\nProbe every plan against these 5 failure classes:\n1. **Network & Router Drops**: Mid-stream SSE/HTTP disconnect, `9router` `401` token expiry, DNS timeout, and duplicate retries.\n2. **Android / Proot Host Limits**: Background process kill (`signal 9`), missing `/sdcard` permission, `LD_PRELOAD` collision, and low-RAM pressure.\n3. **Concurrency & State Races**: Rapid double-taps, screen rotation/recomposition mid-flight, and out-of-order async responses.\n4. **Malformed / Boundary Inputs**: Empty strings, 10MB payloads, non-UTF8 bytes across JNI, and zero/negative layout dimensions.\n5. **Missing Secrets**: PR/CI runs without keystore or API secret env vars.\n\n## 2. Hard Invariants\n- **NEVER** accept \"happy path only\" designs; write concrete fallback behavior for every exposed failure mode into `spec.md`.\n",
