    content: "---\nname: implement-spec\ndescription: Execute an approved spec.md in strict dependency order, preventing scope drift and verifying every acceptance criterion.\nwhen_not_to_use: Exploratory debugging without a spec or open-ended brainstorming.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [execute spec.md, bottom-up build, acceptance criteria, approved spec]\n---\n# Implement Spec (v3)\n\n## 1. Dependency-Ordered Execution\n1. **Parse `spec.md`**: Extract target file map, data contracts, edge cases, and acceptance checks before editing code.\n2. **Build Bottom-Up**: Implement in strict order: `Data Models / Types -> Core Domain / Rust FFI -> IO / Network -> UI -> Tests`.\n3. **Checkpoint Each Milestone**: Compile or run targeted tests after each layer before moving to the next.\n\n## 2. Drift & Blocker Protocol\n- **Spec Conflict**: If a hidden platform constraint breaks `spec.md`, stop coding, update `spec.md` with the minimal adjustment, then resume.\n- **Anti-Bloat**: Keep changes strictly scoped to files listed in `spec.md`; do not refactor unrelated modules mid-flight.\n\n## 3. Hard Invariants & Verification Gate\n- **NEVER** mark a task done with partial `TODO` stubs or skipped edge-case fallbacks.\n- **Verification**: Cross-check every bullet in `spec.md` Acceptance Criteria with passing build/test output and `git status`.\n",
