    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: master-prompt-architect\ndescription: Engineer ultra-dense, zero-ambiguity Master Prompts for OpenCode, Pi, AntiGravity IDE, /swarm workers, and UI prototyping tools.\nwhen_not_to_use: Direct code execution inside the current repo when no external agent handoff is needed.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [master prompt, swarm prompt, ownedfiles, agent prompt, ai studio]\n---\n# Master Prompt Architect (v3)\n\n## 1. Select Target Execution Mode\n- **Mode A — UI Prototype (AI Studio / Web Preview)**:\n  - Lock 100% client-side mocked state (forbid real `localhost` fetches, auth walls, or dead buttons).\n  - Centralize all colors, spacing, typography, and spring configs in `src/tokens.ts`.\n  - Enforce mobile-first constraints: zero horizontal overflow at `375px`, minimum `44px` tap targets, and `font-mono tabular-nums` on all live counters/timers/ports.\n  - Hard cap: under `300 lines` per component file.\n- **Mode B — Single-Agent Surgical Build/Fix (OpenCode / Pi / AntiGravity)**:\n  - Cite exact file paths, symbol/function names, dependency versions, and stacktrace lines.\n  - Hard cap: under `400 lines` per file; split domain, state, and UI cleanly.\n- **Mode C — Parallel `/swarm` Orchestration**:\n  - Partition workers with strictly disjoint `ownedFiles` lists (zero overlap).\n  - Defer shared files (`build.gradle.kts`, `AndroidManifest.xml`, `package.json`, JNI bridges) to the final single-threaded Fan-In merge step.\n\n## 2. Mandatory 4-Block Master Prompt Template\nOutput the prompt inside ONE clean fenced `markdown` block (written in concise technical English for maximum token efficiency):\n1. **Context & Grounding**: Exact files/specs (`AGENTS.md`, `spec.md`, logs) to inspect first.\n2. **Numbered Execution Scope**: Atomic, verifiable tasks ordered by dependency layer.\n3. **Guardrails & Invariants**: Explicit `DO NOT` rules, line caps, and error-handling laws.\n4. **Completion & Stop Condition**: Exact verification command and stop boundary (e.g., stop after `git commit` without infinite polling).\n\n## 3. Hard Invariants\n- **NEVER** emit `TODO` placeholders, unverified library versions, or vague wishes (\"make it cleaner/faster\").\n",
