    summary: "Guide multi-step environment setups, migrations, and deployments with mobile-safe commands, verification signals, and recovery steps.",
    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: wizard\ndescription: Guide multi-step environment setups, migrations, and deployments with mobile-safe commands, verification signals, and recovery steps.\nwhen_not_to_use: Code architecture design or automated diff auditing.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [step-by-step setup, onboarding guide, install walkthrough, migration steps]\n---\n# Wizard (v3)\n\n## 1. Step Design Standards\n- **Mobile Copy-Paste Safe**: Keep each step's command self-contained and newline-safe (`;` / `&&`) so terminal pastes never split mid-argument.\n- **Explicit Verification Signal**: Pair every step with an observable success check (expected stdout, exit code `0`, HTTP `200`, or file size).\n- **Immediate Recovery Path**: Include the exact 1-line fix when a known environment blocker (`LD_PRELOAD`, missing library, DNS, permission denied) occurs.\n\n## 2. Hard Invariants\n- **NEVER** chain more than 3 unrelated setup phases into one blind block without an intermediate verification check.\n",
