    content: "---\nname: writing-for-agents\ndescription: Author dense, token-efficient AGENTS.md and SKILL.md modules with deterministic triggers and verifiable completion gates.\nwhen_not_to_use: User-facing README.md docs or application source code.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [author skill.md, write agents.md, compress prompt, frontmatter]\n---\n# Writing For Agents (v3)\n\n## 1. Token & Structure Standards\n- **Optimal Density**: Keep each `SKILL.md` between `16-30 lines` (`~180-300 tokens`) so multiple skills load simultaneously without starving context windows.\n- **High-Signal Frontmatter**: Write `description` with exact trigger nouns, file extensions, and error symptoms for deterministic agent routing.\n- **Actionable Sections**: Structure body into `Failure Signature -> Fix Matrix`, `Execution Protocol`, and `Hard Invariants & Verification Gate`.\n\n## 2. Hard Invariants\n- **FORBIDDEN**: Filler introductions, motivational fluff, vague advice (\"write clean code\"), or unverified version numbers.\n- **Imperative Precision**: Use `MUST`, `NEVER`, `FORBIDDEN`, exact file paths, and runnable verification commands.\n",
